{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788604",
      "title": "Legacy Angular: Using ngFor & ngIf",
      "lectureOrder": 44,
      "videoOrder": 40,
      "sourceHash": "c01e4d0f3ef8133bc2335d7f5aa8efb2c3ef2f4a307571f2d66d6b78220471e9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "In the previous lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "you learned about @for and @if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "Now, this syntax is relatively new though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "It was only added with Angular version 17.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "Earlier versions of Angular don't support this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 19.98,
          "en": "And, of course, it's possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.98,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "that you are working on a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "that's using such an older Angular version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 30.03,
          "en": "In that case, there is an alternative syntax, which used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "to be the standard before the introduction of @for and @if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "And that syntax would look like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 42.68,
          "en": "You would add *ngFor on the element that should be repeated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "and then add an equal sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "and between the quotes have this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "for repeating the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "Though you would have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 58.73,
          "en": "to add the keyword let in front of this user variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.76,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "Now this *ngFor thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "is a so-called structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "Now, structural directives are, in the end, enhancements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "you could say, that you can add to elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 75.12,
          "en": "that will change those elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.12,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "or change the DOM where those elements are used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 82.71000000000001,
          "en": "and we'll dive deeper into directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "and how you can build your own directives later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 87.243,
          "en": "in a dedicated course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 92.55,
          "en": "In order to use this *ngFor structural directive here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.55,
          "end": 96.78,
          "en": "you have to go to the component class of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 99.13,
          "en": "where you want to use it in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.87,
          "en": "and add it here to the imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 106.113,
          "en": "For that, you first of all have to import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "You have to import NgFor,r written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "from @angular/common,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "so not from core but from common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "And then add it here to this imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 124.71,
          "en": "This is how you unlock this structural directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.71,
          "end": 126.603,
          "en": "for use in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.16,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "And it's similar for if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 135.68,
          "en": "Instead of using @if, so I'll comment this out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "you would add *ngIf on the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 142.36,
          "en": "that should be shown conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "and then put your condition between those quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 149.43,
          "en": "So for example, selectedUser, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "Now, in this case, TypeScript actually doesn't understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "that here selectedUser will be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "and hence, I would need to add an exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.48,
          "en": "to convince it that this is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.48,
          "end": 165.3,
          "en": "For showing the else case, you would have to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.3,
          "end": 170.01,
          "en": "for a more complex syntax where you add a special element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.01,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "the ng-template element, which is an element provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 176.25,
          "en": "out of the box by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.25,
          "end": 180.33,
          "en": "and you would wrap that around your else content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 183.48,
          "en": "and then go back to *ngIf, add a semicolon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.48,
          "end": 185.53,
          "en": "and then add the else keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.39,
          "end": 190.59,
          "en": "and then give this ng-template here an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 195.48,
          "en": "by adding #fallback or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "The name after the hashtag is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "and then you refer to that name hereafter else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 207.933,
          "en": "So that's how this else content here is displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "Now, just like *ngFor, *ngIf must be unlocked first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 213.84,
          "en": "before you can use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.84,
          "end": 216.16,
          "en": "So you also have to import *ngIf",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 220.353,
          "en": "and then add it here to this imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 223.82999999999998,
          "en": "And with that done, if you now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.82999999999998,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "you got the same behavior as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "but now in a way that also works in older Angular versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 232.703,
          "en": "with *ngFor and *ngIf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "Now, of course, this course here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 240.21,
          "en": "is about teaching you the recent Angular versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "and hence, I'll not use *ngFor and *ngIf,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 248.93,
          "en": "also because as you can tell, this approach is more verbose,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.97,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "especially here with *ngIf and this else block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 255.813,
          "en": "but also with all those extra imports that are needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 256.83,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll get rid of those imports here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 262.08299999999997,
          "en": "and also of these imports at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 264.39,
          "end": 269.07,
          "en": "and I'll get rid of the *ngIf directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 269.07,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "and this #fallback wrapper ng-template here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.79,
          "en": "and I'll bring back @if instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 278.103,
          "en": "and this else block like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 279.72,
          "end": 281.7,
          "en": "and do the same for *ngFor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "Delete it here on the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 287.25,
          "en": "and instead bring back @for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.25,
          "end": 288.48,
          "en": "And now also get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.48,
          "end": 290.64,
          "en": "of this exclamation mark down here again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.64,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "because now we don't need it anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.4,
          "en": "because this is the recommended way of outputting list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 296.4,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "or conditional content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 298.08,
          "end": 301.56,
          "en": "But since you might be working on an Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 301.56,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "that uses an older version of Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 307.29,
          "en": "or you simply might stumble across *ngFor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 307.29,
          "end": 311.4,
          "en": "or *ngIf on existing projects, it is, of course, important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 311.4,
          "end": 314.88,
          "en": "to also understand how those directives work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 314.88,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "and how you could use them for outputting list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 319.323,
          "en": "or conditional content.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
